   "attributes": {
    "Science": "It found the Moon rings for a long time after an impact \u2014 evidence of a dry, fractured crust. It ran for three weeks before overheating.",
    "Title": "Passive Seismic Experiment (EASEP)",
    "What": "A solar-powered seismometer, levelled by hand on the regolith and shielded from the Sun.",
    "Why": "To listen for moonquakes and meteorite strikes, and use them to read the Moon's interior the way an X-ray reads a body.",
